          "handle": "jukan05",
          "platform": "X",
          "text": "I think the market ultimately has no choice but to go sell memory, long optical in the \"short term.\" Actually, some hedge funds already seem to have this position on.  There are three main reasons.  1. With Korean leveraged ETFs effectively dead, LPs are in a redemption rush,",
          "url": "https://x.com/jukan05/status/2086068556148683040",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-08T20:34:35.000+08:00",
          "interaction": 4055
        },
        {
          "handle": "jukan05",
          "platform": "X",
          "text": "Sounds like Apple is expecting further memory chip price hikes in the coming quarters:  Apple earnings call: \"Let me back up and talk about memory in general, because I know this is a subject on many of your minds. If you look at, as I'd said on the last call, we paid more for",
          "url": "https://x.com/jukan05/status/2083033961786490913",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-31T11:36:12.000+08:00",
          "interaction": 2822
        },
        {
          "handle": "jukan05",
          "platform": "X",
          "text": "Micron and Meta have jointly published a white paper, and it contains some truly important insights. It’s definitely worth reading.   https:// micron.com/about/blog/mem ory/dram/when-memory-changes-the-equation …",
          "url": "https://x.com/jukan05/status/2081243127797686457",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-26T13:00:03.000+08:00",
          "interaction": 2322
        },
        {
          "handle": "jukan05",
          "platform": "X",
          "text": "Apple is peddling the bullshit argument that iPhone prices directly affect inflation and that it needs to use Chinese-made memory to keep inflation low. Yet even though the fivefold increase in memory prices raised its costs by only about $50, Apple increased prices by $250. Cut",
          "url": "https://x.com/jukan05/status/2080822662180536721",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-25T09:09:17.000+08:00",
          "interaction": 2037
        },
        {
          "handle": "jukan05",
          "platform": "X",
          "text": "Citi cuts Micron price target on peaking memory prices  Citi downgraded Micron, arguing that both DRAM and NAND prices will see QoQ gains decelerate over the next four quarters, with pricing peaking in the May (F2Q) quarter of next year.  Specifically, Citi revised its QoQ DRAM",
          "url": "https://x.com/jukan05/status/2085865896090992746",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-08T07:09:17.000+08:00",
          "interaction": 2009
        },
        {
          "handle": "jukan05",
          "platform": "X",
          "text": "Just in from The Wall Street Journal: Apple is lobbying the White House to allow the use of Chinese-made memory chips, while Micron is pushing back hard, arguing that it should never be permitted—putting the two companies at odds.",
          "url": "https://x.com/jukan05/status/2080821984385278397",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-25T09:06:35.000+08:00",
          "interaction": 1568
        },
        {
          "handle": "jukan05",
          "platform": "X",
          "text": "I came across an interesting analysis today. It argued that while the unwinding of leveraged positions has contributed to the recent decline in memory stocks, the market is also beginning to price in the prospect of future supply expansion.  The argument goes as follows. Even if",
          "url": "https://x.com/jukan05/status/2078462124486283755",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-18T20:49:21.000+08:00",
          "interaction": 1554
        },
        {
          "handle": "jukan05",
          "platform": "X",
          "text": "There’s a reason for the saying that, when it comes to memory semiconductors, you shouldn’t trust anyone but Korean analysts, lol.  KIS is a veteran in this field.  Not only KIS, but veteran analysts at Citi, Meritz, and elsewhere all lowered their earnings estimates for SK",
          "url": "https://x.com/jukan05/status/2082242051173937333",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-29T07:09:25.000+08:00",
          "interaction": 1439
        }
